{
    "name": "E2E SurveyMonkey - new response trigger",
    "description": "Lists the responses of the permanent E2E survey, sends the New Response trigger a response_completed event for the latest one, signed with the secret of the webhook the trigger registered, and asserts the emitted response and Get Response with their answers.",
    "notes": {
        "ca1fa269-f9ee-4b52-92b2-8b93bff12a09": {
            "x": 64,
            "y": 624,
            "width": 1040,
            "height": 368,
            "content": "## ⚠️ Test data assumption, self-provoked trigger\n\nThe flow needs a permanent survey in the E2E account: **529066657** (\"E2E SurveyMonkey - permanent survey (do not delete)\") with one single-textbox question, the web link collector **466427749** and completed responses whose answer is `E2E answer`. On a fresh account: create the survey and a web link collector, open the collector URL, answer `E2E answer`, click Done, then put the survey and collector IDs into the trigger, List Responses, Get Response, the event body and the Asserts.\n\n`NewResponse.start()` registers a real `response_completed` webhook for that survey, and `stop()` deletes it. The event itself does not come from SurveyMonkey: the app has no `responses_write` scope, so a flow cannot submit a response, and on the E2E account (Basic plan, draft app) SurveyMonkey delivers no webhook events at all (probed 2026-11-18 with a response submitted through the collector page).\n\nThe provoke lane therefore takes the latest response from List Responses, lists the webhooks, picks the one named `Appmixer New Response <trigger id>`, reads its `authorization` secret back from SurveyMonkey and POSTs an event in SurveyMonkey's documented shape to the trigger's own webhook URL. The trigger checks the secret and reads the response with its answers from the API."
        }
    },
